From d223ad3a0f224350377394ced5a5056ed15dadab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 02:28:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 195/256] perf(cpu): release dead SSA values in the SVE256
 launch loop

Reuse backends/cpu/ssa_liveness.py (plan_release + release_dead_values)
exactly like the AVX2/AVX-512 launch loops: parameters and returns stay
pinned, a value is dropped strictly after its last consumer returns, and
a never-consumed non-return value is dropped right after production.

Tests: SVE256 liveness release-point parity with the AVX-512 schedule,
release-enabled/release-disabled bit-identical A/B plus scalar oracle,
and a spy test proving caller-owned TypedByteView buffers are only ever
parameter-pinned and never released.  The layout/indexing focused suites
gain the same PYPTO_X_SVE_TEST_MODE=native switch the W8A8 suite already
has (default stays qemu), and the driver A/B tool can now disable the
SVE256 release for the whole-net differential.
